# Copy to deploy/homelab/.env (gitignored) and fill in. deploy.sh reads it as KEY=value lines (nothing is executed);
# a variable set in the shell wins over this file. The repository root .env (docker compose) is not used here.
# Placeholders only: never commit real values.

# --- Where to deploy: required, no defaults (deploy.sh stops and lists the ones that are missing) ---
# Registry host and project the images are pushed to and pulled from (e.g. registry.example.com/lotties).
REGISTRY=<registry-host>/<project>
# Kube context passed to every kubectl/helm call (e.g. my-cluster); in-cluster: a pod's own service account.
KUBE_CONTEXT=<kube-context>
# Ingress class of the public entry (e.g. traefik).
INGRESS_CLASS=<ingress-class>
# cert-manager ClusterIssuer of the certificate (e.g. letsencrypt-production). Set it empty for no certificate annotation.
CLUSTER_ISSUER=<cluster-issuer>
# docker-registry Secret (in NS) the pods pull the images with (e.g. registry-pull).
PULL_SECRET=<pull-secret-name>
# Optional: a namespace that already holds PULL_SECRET; when it is missing in NS it is copied from there
# (COPY_PULL_SECRET=1, or a yes). Empty or left out: a missing pull Secret stops the run with the command to create it.
# PULL_SECRET_SOURCE_NS=<namespace>

# --- Where to deploy: optional (these are the defaults) ---
# NS=lotties-app-production
# PUBLIC_HOST=lotties.app
# TLS_SECRET=lotties-tls

# --- Identity provider (Keycloak realm lotties.app at https://auth.lotties.app); defaults shown ---
# AUTH_AUTHORITY=https://auth.lotties.app/realms/lotties.app
# AUTH_AUDIENCE=lotties-api
# Account deletion (store requirement): a confidential client of the realm with a service account that may delete users
# (realm-management role manage-users). Both or none; with none, deleting an account in the app keeps the Keycloak
# user and the app tells the user so. Setup and rotation: docs/KEYCLOAK-ACCOUNT-DELETION.md. Kept in the Secret lotties-secrets.
# AUTH_ADMIN_CLIENT_ID=lotties-account-deletion
# AUTH_ADMIN_CLIENT_SECRET=<admin-client-secret>

# --- Web build arguments: public, baked into the JavaScript bundle (a change rebuilds the web image) ---
# Required: the public SPA client id of the realm.
VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=<spa-client-id>
# Default: AUTH_AUTHORITY. Its origin is allowed in the CSP connect-src.
# VITE_OIDC_AUTHORITY=
# Keycloak: leave empty (an audience mapper puts lotties-api in the token). Auth0: the API identifier.
# VITE_OIDC_AUDIENCE=
# Leave empty: same origin (the Ingress sends /api to the API).
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
# Source repository link in the landing footer (AGPL source offer); empty hides it.
# Setting it at the public flip turns on the footer and About "Source code on GitHub" link, and with it the default
# "Report a problem" link (<repository>/issues/new).
# VITE_REPO_URL=https://github.com/<owner>/<repository>
# "Report a problem" link (http/https). Left out = VITE_REPO_URL + /issues/new, else a mailto: to
# VITE_PRIVACY_CONTACT_EMAIL, else hidden.
# VITE_ISSUES_URL=https://github.com/<owner>/<repository>/issues/new
# "Support Lotties" link (http/https only; a link out, never a payment in the app; docs/design/43-funding-options.md).
# Left out hides it.
# VITE_SUPPORT_URL=https://<your support page>
# "Get the phone app" beta links on the landing page (http/https; each left out hides its card, step or button; all
# left out hides the section; docs/DEPLOY.md "Phone app links").
# VITE_TESTFLIGHT_URL=https://testflight.apple.com/join/<code>
# VITE_ANDROID_TESTERS_GROUP_URL=https://groups.google.com/g/<group>
# VITE_ANDROID_OPTIN_URL=https://play.google.com/apps/testing/app.lotties.app
# VITE_PLAY_STORE_URL=https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=app.lotties.app
# Privacy policy contacts on https://lotties.app/privacy (public). Left out = the policy's defaults (the project
# maintainers, the GitHub issue tracker). Set them before a store submission: docs/PRIVACY-OWNER-CHECKLIST.md.
# VITE_PRIVACY_CONTROLLER_NAME=<controller name as published>
# VITE_PRIVACY_CONTACT_EMAIL=<privacy contact email>
# VITE_PRIVACY_DPO=<encarregado: name and/or email>

# --- Database (the Secret lotties-secrets). A key left out keeps what the Secret already has; set to empty to remove it ---
DB_HOST=<postgres-host>
DB_PORT=5432
DB_NAME=lotties
# The API's limited role (docs/DEPLOY.md "Database roles"; e.g. lotties_app).
DB_APP_USER=<app-role>
DB_APP_PASSWORD=<app-role-password>

# Opt-in: the API applies pending migrations at start with the migrator role. The pod then holds the migrator
# credentials (see README.md "Migrations"). Default false.
# DB_AUTO_MIGRATE=false
# DB_MIGRATOR_USER=<migrator-role>
# DB_MIGRATOR_PASSWORD=<migrator-role-password>

# --- Web Push (optional): all three or none. Generate a pair once: dotnet run --project code/api/src/Lotties.Api -- --generate-vapid-keys
# PUSH_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=<public-key>
# PUSH_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=<private-key>
# PUSH_VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:<operator@example.com>

# --- Try-it demo (optional): a random value of 32+ characters turns the demo on, none keeps it off (docs/design/45-try-it-demo.md).
# Generate one: openssl rand -base64 48
# DEMO_SIGNING_KEY=<random-32+-characters>

# --- Silent pushes for the widgets (optional, off by default; docs/DEPLOY.md "Silent pushes for the widgets") ---
# Keep SILENT_PUSH_ENABLED off until the privacy policy text in docs/legal-held/widget-silent-push/ is released.
# The flag is not a secret: left out it is false (a deploy without it turns silent pushes off). With true, the run stops
# unless one channel below is complete. The keys go only to the Secret lotties-secrets; a key left out keeps what the
# Secret has; set to empty to remove it. Each value is one line (the .p8 text or the service-account JSON as base64).
# SILENT_PUSH_ENABLED=false
# APNs: all three or none (PUSH_APNS_BUNDLE_ID is optional, default app.lotties.app).
# PUSH_APNS_KEY_ID=<apns-key-id>
# PUSH_APNS_TEAM_ID=<apple-team-id>
# PUSH_APNS_KEY_P8=<base64-of-the-p8-file>
# PUSH_APNS_BUNDLE_ID=app.lotties.app
# FCM: both or none.
# PUSH_FCM_PROJECT_ID=<firebase-project-id>
# PUSH_FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=<base64-of-the-service-account-json>

# --- Bring your own database (optional, off by default; docs/DEPLOY.md "Bring your own database: turning it on") ---
# Every value goes only to the Secret lotties-secrets. A key left out keeps what the Secret has; set to empty to remove it.
# With Stores__Enabled=true the run stops unless Stores__CurrentKeyId names a key below that is base64 of exactly 32 bytes.
# Stores__Enabled=false
# Accounts that may use it (users.id guid or OIDC sub, comma-separated, at most 100). Empty = nobody.
# Stores__Allowlist=<owner-user-id-or-sub>
# Stores__CurrentKeyId=k1
# One line per key-encryption key; generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32. Keep old keys until no row uses them.
# Stores__KeyEncryptionKeys__k1=<base64-of-32-random-bytes>

# --- Proxies whose X-Forwarded-For/-Proto the API trusts (CIDR list). Default: the private ranges, which cover the pod network ---
# FORWARDED_HEADERS_TRUSTED_NETWORKS=10.42.0.0/16

# --- Browser origins allowed to call the API (comma-separated). Default: https://<PUBLIC_HOST> only ---
# The iOS/Android app (code/mobile) calls the API from its WebView origins: add them when it ships.
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://lotties.app,https://localhost,capacitor://localhost

# --- Build options ---
# TAG=
# FORCE_BUILD=1
# SKIP_BUILD=1
# VERSION=1.0.0
# COPY_PULL_SECRET=1
